                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c28d41e-4722-3947-9fc8-ced9970f85a0",
                        "entry_id": "6667c798-bdc4-3aba-a37d-543f8854424e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "politisch-geografischer Begriff für das Staatsgebiet der Volksrepublik China ohne Hong Kong und Macau; im Gegensatz zu Inselchina, womit Hong Kong, Macau sowie das von der Republik China kontrollierte Territorium auf der Insel Taiwan (früher: Formosa) und vorgelagerter Inseln zusammengefasst werden"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "033366fb-308c-461d-a99e-b060467e17fa",
                                "sense_id": "5c28d41e-4722-3947-9fc8-ced9970f85a0",
                                "text": "„Der schwache Abschluss erfolgte nach einem steilen Anstieg zum Handelsauftakt um sogar mehr als 7 Prozent, der aber nur sehr kurzlebig war. Während die Krise in Griechenland auf den weitgehend abgeschotteten chinesischen Aktienmärkten keine Rolle spielt, beendete in Hongkong der Hang Seng Index vor dem Hintergrund des griechischen Referendums und der Aktienkrise in Festlandchina die Morgensitzung deutlich niedriger um 3,18 Prozent im Minus. Mit einem energischen Eingreifen hatte die Regierung in Peking über das Wochenende versucht, Vertrauen wiederherzustellen und einen weiteren Kursrutsch zu verhindern.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90a6c275-d569-416f-b8dd-62d58698358b",
                        "source_entry_id": "6667c798-bdc4-3aba-a37d-543f8854424e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5c28d41e-4722-3947-9fc8-ced9970f85a0",
                        "target_lang_word": "mainland China",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mainland China",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                        "entry_id": "691b2649-f2ca-3d19-991e-1593d6ae5add",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The People's Republic of China, viewed as the general geographical region administered by the PRC in the aftermath of the Chinese Civil War (as opposed to Hong Kong, Macau, and Taiwan which are coastal and insular areas)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bdc96e1-d5f4-4d6a-a4df-44348d0c8099",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "Had my Government remained on the mainland, there would never have been such calamities as the Korean War and the Communist occupation of northern Korea and northern Indo-China. The place to begin combating Communism in Asia, therefore, is mainland China."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "857a81eb-b638-4b81-a44a-a6111064ba6f",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "In 1953 the city had only 20% of the total value of mainland China's industrial output, but this was officially claimed to be 368% higher than that of 1950."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc0ee63e-155d-4dbb-a212-4a35a69dcf2d",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "Many Americans were primarily Europeanists in their approach to foreign affairs, dismissing Asia as relatively unimportant. But the United States is a Pacific power, and rapid changes were taking place in Asia—where more than half the human race lived—that might well determine the world's future. Japan would soon be the world's third-ranking industrial power, behind the United States and the Soviet Union. Some of the most rapid rates of economic progress anywhere were being achieved by the nations of non-Communist Asia. And mainland China potentially posed the greatest threat to peace during the final third of the twentieth century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61d5893b-53d4-4cf9-8e8e-554cb7c79acb",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "Chinese Communist rule on mainland China during the past three decades has destroyed the vitality, spirit and cultural heritage of the Chinese people, said Fox Butterfield, during an address at Sun Yat-sen Memorial Hall Dec. 11."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcb00c4b-b235-453f-8ad4-3f372636e727",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "At Cihhu (Cihu), near the town of Dasi (Daxi), 30 miles (50 km) southwest of Taipei on Provincial Highway 7, Chiang Kai-shek lies entombed above ground in a granite and marble coffin in one of his former country villas. The gravesite is \"temporary,\" as before his death Chiang had requested his body be returned to his native province of Zhejiang in mainland China."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8652ed64-a74d-489f-bf50-eabf09954a78",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "Tsuen Wan is a working-class area near Hong Kong’s border with the Chinese mainland, miles from the city’s gleaming financial district."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6c25365-ddb9-447c-9800-16d5d1700ee2",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "It’s hard to imagine now, but there were once three mountainous, verdant islands between Macau and mainland China. The Portuguese named them Dom João, Montanha and Lapa. Later the islands became known in Chinese as Xiao (Little) Hengqin, Da (Big) Hengqin and Wanzai, respectively."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66876961-60d6-466e-8df4-aa5133189729",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "Hong Kong and mainland China are among few places in the world still aiming to suppress every COVID-19 outbreak, but the Omicron variant has proven tough to keep under control."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e5e69b7-fa93-474b-aca9-6c3acbacc346",
                                                "sense_id": "9df8255a-84c3-3f67-8148-291ea8d0cdf4",
                                                "text": "In mainland China, authorities have shut down travel out of and within the hardest-hit province, Jilin in the northeast. More than 1,800 cases were reported in Jilin on Friday, out of 2,400 nationwide. Restrictions were partially eased, however, in Shenzhen, a major tech and finance hub bordering Hong Kong that had been locked down since Sunday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04f1a75f-2c0b-325c-89c5-20eb808c2212",
                                        "entry_id": "691b2649-f2ca-3d19-991e-1593d6ae5add",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Also used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see mainland, China."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57444022-db8b-4ce5-81b0-292bb19d5b18",
                                                "sense_id": "04f1a75f-2c0b-325c-89c5-20eb808c2212",
                                                "text": "“Tourists could come to Hainan before going to places such as Vietnam, Cambodia, Indonesia and Singapore, and shop offshore duty-free products which could be directly delivered back home, each person can purchase as much as 100,000 yuan (US$15,255),” Shen said.\nTourists from Southeast Asian countries could also be inclined to visit Hainan before touring mainland China, he said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
